      rationale: "Sudden coma with pinpoint pupils (interrupted descending sympathetic fibers), loss of horizontal eye movements (pontine gaze center and [[mlf|medial longitudinal fasciculus]]), [[decerebrate-posturing|extensor posturing]], and irregular breathing is the picture of a pontine lesion, classically a hypertensive pontine hemorrhage. Preserved vertical responses show the midbrain is still working. No response to naloxone argues against opioids.",
